  "query_preview": "..\nWhile only isolated showers are visible on satellite this afternoon,\nthe Marianas sits along a convergence zone between TD Jangmi and the\neasterly trade winds. With the addition of plenty of moisture and \nupper level instability, this is expected to allow for the \ndevelopment of scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms tonight \nthrough at least tomorrow while Jangmi remains nearby. Precipitation \nchances will begin decreasing Friday night as Jangmi moves away and \nthe convergence zone drifts off to the west. A dryer, weak trade wind\nflow is expected to take it's place and will bring isolated showers \nfor the rest of the forecast period.",
